1
00:03:43,846 --> 00:03:49,846
They came in peace, they left in chaos.

2
00:07:27,692 --> 00:07:33,692
The Angry Birds Movie is a animation, adventure,
comedy film directed by Clay Kaytis.

3
00:11:11,538 --> 00:11:17,538
An island populated entirely by happy, flightless birds or almost entirely.

4
00:14:55,384 --> 00:15:01,384
In this paradise, Red, a bird with a temper problem, speedy Chuck,
and the volatile Bomb have always been outsiders.

5
00:18:39,230 --> 00:18:45,230
But when the island is visited by mysterious green piggies, it’s up to
these unlikely outcasts to figure out what the pigs are up to.

6
00:22:23,076 --> 00:22:29,076
Red (voice), played by Jason Sudeikis.

7
00:26:06,923 --> 00:26:12,923
Chuck (voice), played by Josh Gad.

8
00:29:50,769 --> 00:29:56,769
Bomb (voice), played by Danny McBride.

9
00:33:34,615 --> 00:33:40,615
Matilda (voice), played by Maya Rudolph.

10
00:37:18,461 --> 00:37:24,461
Leonard (voice), played by Bill Hader.

11
00:41:02,307 --> 00:41:08,307
Mighty Eagle (voice), played by Peter Dinklage.

12
00:44:46,153 --> 00:44:52,153
The Angry Birds Movie is a 2016 animated comedy film
based on the Angry Birds video game series.

13
00:48:30,000 --> 00:48:36,000
It was directed by Clay Kaytis and Fergal Reilly, and written by Jon Vitti.

14
00:52:13,846 --> 00:52:19,846
It features the voices of Jason Sudeikis, Josh Gad, Danny McBride, Maya Rudolph, Kate
McKinnon, Sean Penn, Tony Hale, Keegan-Michael Key, Bill Hader, and Peter Dinklage.

15
00:55:57,692 --> 00:56:03,692
The film follows Red, an outcast on an island of anthropomorphic flightless birds, as he suspects a newly arrived crew of pigs, led by
Leonard, of plotting an evil plan, and attempts to put a stop to them with the help of his newfound friends Chuck and Bomb.

16
00:59:41,538 --> 00:59:47,538
After the success of the Angry Birds Toons animated series, Rovio Entertainment, the
developer of the original video game, began work on a film adaptation.

17
01:03:25,384 --> 01:03:31,384
The project was announced in December 2012.

18
01:07:09,230 --> 01:07:15,230
The first image from the film was revealed in October 2014, with Sudeikis, Gad, McBride,
Hader, Rudolph, and Dinklage revealed to be part of its cast at the same time.

19
01:10:53,076 --> 01:10:59,076
Rovio and Sony Pictures announced they would spend roughly €100 million on the marketing and distribution of
The Angry Birds Movie, becoming the most expensive Finnish-produced film up to that point.

20
01:14:36,923 --> 01:14:42,923
Sony Pictures Imageworks was responsible for
handling animation services for the film.

21
01:18:20,769 --> 01:18:26,769
The Angry Birds Movie was released in the United States on
May 20, 2016, by Sony Pictures Releasing.

22
01:22:04,615 --> 01:22:10,615
The film received mixed reviews from critics and grossed $352 million.

23
01:25:48,461 --> 01:25:54,461
A sequel, The Angry Birds Movie 2, was released in 2019, and a third
film, The Angry Birds Movie 3, is scheduled for 2026.

24
01:29:32,307 --> 01:29:38,307
The film explores themes of island, pig, villain, eagle, rivalry.

25
01:33:16,153 --> 01:33:22,153
The tone is lighthearted.
